course: dictionary
lesson: 4701
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word honeycomb is a good example. It can be a bees' wax home, a sweet toffee, a pattern of six-sided shapes, or a verb meaning full of holes. Read the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: «Honeycomb cells are hexagons, which hold the most honey for the least wax.» Here honeycomb means the wax structure that bees build, because the sentence talks about cells, honey and wax. The clues are the bees' cells and the honey inside them.
explain: «A hill honeycombed with caves» uses honeycombed as a verb. It does not mean the hill is made of wax or toffee. The word caves is the clue: the hill is full of holes and tunnels. Always check your chosen meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A honeycomb is a wax structure made by bees, with many six-sided cells.
fact: Bees store honey in the cells of a honeycomb and raise their young there.
fact: «Honeycomb» can also mean a sweet, crunchy, golden toffee full of bubbles.
fact: A honeycomb pattern is made of hexagons, and hexagons fit together with no gaps.
fact: To be «honeycombed» with something means to be full of holes or tunnels.
exercise: «Honeycomb cells are hexagons, which hold the most honey for the least wax.» What shape are the cells? | A star | A circle | *A hexagon | A square with rounded corners
exercise: «A toucan's huge beak is light because it is a honeycomb of bone covered with keratin.» What does honeycomb mean here? | *A structure full of tiny holes and spaces, like a bee's wax | A jar of honey from the shop | A hard, flat shell | A sweet, crunchy toffee
exercise: Lily says honeycomb is a crunchy sweet full of bubbles. Which meaning is she using? | *Golden toffee full of bubbles | A bee's home in a tree | A honey jar with a lid | A pattern of circles
test: In maths, a honeycomb pattern fits together with no gaps. What is this called? | Rotating | *Tessellating | Multiplying | Dividing
test: «A hill honeycombed with caves» What does honeycombed mean in this sentence? | Made of honey | Covered in grass | *Full of holes and tunnels | Very tall
exam: «Wax is costly because bees eat a lot of honey to make it.» Why is wax costly for bees? | It is dug up from the ground | It melts in the sun | *Bees must eat a lot of honey to make it | Wax is bought from shops
